# GLXEE README Style

Treat `README.md` as an in-universe GLXEE transmission, not a generic project
README.

- Keep the visual language: pixel-art assets, VOLTEX / UGDF terminology,
  compact status panels, monospace HUD blocks, restrained badges, and dark
  Game Boy–shell presentation.
- Use the canonical order: identity and visual hook, boot, controls, game loop,
  factions / galaxies, Home Station / hangar, combat, feature summary,
  architecture, development waves, documentation, lore, credits.
- Describe each system once in its owning section. Use the Features section
  only as a short index; do not duplicate full explanations there.
- Prefer existing assets from `assets/ui/readme-*.svg` and game sprites over
  invented decorative graphics. Keep image alt text descriptive.
- Document new work in the Development Waves table with a feature ID, concise
  scope, and matching `feat:` / `docs:` commit convention.
- Preserve GitHub readability: short paragraphs, clear headings, small tables,
  fenced monospace panels, valid relative links, and no decorative block wider
  than the normal README content.
- Before finishing a README change, check links, headings, image paths, and
  redundant sections. Keep the README factual and aligned with the codebase.
